# Print-resolution archival masters. These are scans supplied for this signage
# project by the museums and collections credited in NOTICE.md, and are not
# redistributed here. The web-resolution copies the site serves live in
# assets/web/ and ARE committed, so the site builds from a fresh clone.
#
# To rebuild the print PDFs you need the masters locally; they are in the
# project's Google Drive handoff folder.
assets/images/sign-*/*.jpg
assets/images/sign-*/*.jpeg
assets/images/sign-*/*.JPG
assets/images/sign-*/*.JPEG
assets/images/sign-*/*.tif
assets/images/sign-*/*.tiff
extracted-signs/
Existing Mill River Signage*/
Mill River Trail Images for Walks/

# Full-resolution originals of the existing-signage photographs. The readable
# 2000px copies in assets/web/existing/ ARE committed and are the record; the
# originals live in Existing Mill River Signage-1-001.zip.
assets/images/existing/

# Research material shared with the project but not ours to redistribute.
# Sinye Tang's thesis is here because it is useful to read while writing signs,
# not because it belongs to this repo. If anything from it ends up on a sign,
# credit it and ask her first.
docs/*.pdf
